 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Fragments of a youth, far relieved from\nThe burden of this earth's harsh occupation,\nA wasp-brought world has lured him forth into\nThe green and verdant suburb of creation:\nHis life is but one year; the whole duration\nOf which he dwells is all that Heaven\nHath given Him by His gracious creation.\nI have heard them talk on his death's effect\nOn all that were in love with him: indeed\nThere seems an unwept sorrow at our\nConstancy to follow these fragrant leaves\nThrough every flower'd garden. Are",
